"""Atlas content for patches 4.1–4.56, MSQ #502 Arenvald's Adventure to #540 A Brief Reprieve, and the cp-sb-4-56
milestone (after A Requiem for Heroes). Arc tag k. Data only (docs/atlas/era-modules.md is the contract).

Researched 2026-11-19 from the saved Console Games Wiki wikitext (lanes S14 from #502, S16–S22); every locator is an exact
substring of a quest's Journal, Steps or main dialogue (stage directions inside cutscenes included). Spoiler rules this
module follows:
  - the Stormblood cast reuses the contract's conventional IDs (char-hien, char-yotsuyu, char-asahi, char-fordola,
    char-zenos, char-gosetsu, char-arenvald, loc-ala-mhigo, org-ala-mhigan-resistance, org-mol, org-dotharl, org-oronir);
    each first presentation here stands on its own as of its step, and names nobody before that entity's first record here;
  - first names and titles only: no "Aldynn", "Hext" (Lyse's surname, as "Commander Hext"), "Garlond", "Baelsar",
    "Manderville", "zos Galvus", "sas Brutus", "quo Soranus" or "rem Lupis"; the Ironworks, never its full name;
  - Yotsuyu's amnesia is an alias, not a second entity: the player knows her throughout, and Gosetsu names her "Tsuyu"
    from #512; Shadowhunter is the reveal (→ Gaius, #537); the voice and the hooded figure of A Requiem for Heroes are
    one entity (Tataru suspects they are the same), shown by its game label ("Enigmatic Figure"), never its speaker tag;
  - "Emet-Selch" and "the First" stay out of displayed text: the story so far does not need them, so ALLOW is empty.
"""

def P(frm, until, scope, name, summary, claims, aliases=()):
    return dict(frm=frm, until=until, scope=scope, name=name, aliases=list(aliases), summary=summary, claims=claims)

(K502, K503, K504, K505, K506, K507, K508, K509, K510, K511, K512, K513, K514, K515, K516, K517, K518, K519, K520,
 K521, K522, K523, K524, K525, K526, K527, K528, K529, K530, K531, K532, K533, K534, K535, K536, K537, K538, K539,
 K540) = (f"cp-msq-{n}" for n in range(502, 541))
MS = "cp-sb-4-56"

